{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":385943,"duration_api_ms":270448,"ttft_ms":2225,"num_turns":14,"result":"Iteration complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Experiment exp022 — `ragJustifiedQuestions`** (interleaved per-question chain-of-thought)\n\n- **Hypothesis:** exp018's in-schema CoT (name *all 7* critical unknowns first, then write all 7 questions) failed because the model filled the batch list generically and the questions inherited it — a batch list conditions all slots at once but gates none. The untried complement: **interleave** the reasoning so the schema forces a concrete decision-impact rationale *immediately before each question*, with an explicit \"if your rationale is vague, the slot is filler — replace it\" instruction. A per-emission gate should be harder to satisfy with filler.\n- **Result: quality 0.302** (dev-10), spec 100%, 0/0/10. Rubric: atom 4, spec 3, **coverage 3**, nat 3, **nonRed 4**.\n- **Verdict: DISCARDED** — below the plateau (exp011 0.323, exp003 0.320) and below baseline (0.307).\n- **Insight:** Falsified as a coverage lever. The model can fabricate a plausible-sounding concrete rationale for *whatever* generic/niche question it was already going to ask, then asks it — so reasoning-before-asking rationalises the modal output rather than blocking it. Same recurring gaps verbatim (trip misses departure city/dates, tax stays generic-procedural, etc.). The interleave *did* hold non-redundancy at 4 (modest gain vs exp011/exp018's 3), but compound option-lists leaked into questions and the headline landed below baseline. This closes the in-schema-CoT angle from **both** framings (batch-leading list exp018 + interleaved exp022).\n\nBuild green; exactly one new run (exp022) logged to `results/runs.jsonl`; program.md updated. The plateau (exp003/exp011 ~0.32) holds; the only genuinely untried lever remains the weight-level LoRA adapter, not runnable in a single invocation.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0b9e096-ee6a-440a-8c11-659c6cba2833","total_cost_usd":1.36947725,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87623,"cache_read_input_tokens":725559,"output_tokens":18335,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87623},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":87252,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1755,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":18335,"cacheReadInputTokens":725559,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87623,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3689182500000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"49cc50f5-56f5-4b8b-b211-971eb3d6c55c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":426652,"duration_api_ms":310047,"ttft_ms":2443,"num_turns":32,"result":"Done. One complete autoresearch iteration:\n\n**exp023 — scoped starting-point critique** (the rules-endorsed \"smarter multi-FM: scope a critique to ONE named failure mode\"). Stage 1 was the exp011 contrastive-RAG draft (current best); stage 2 was a single call judging *only* whether any of the 7 slots establishes the user's starting point (the dominant recurring miss across the whole dev set), with the fix applied surgically in Swift — at most one slot swapped, the other six verbatim, filler/near-dup defended.\n\n**Result: quality 0.273** — a regression (−0.050 vs the exp011 best, −0.034 vs baseline). Build was green; one new run logged (#24).\n\n**Honest verdict — falsified, and informative:** even a single-failure-mode, single-slot-swap critique loses. The starting-point gaps persisted *verbatim* in the judge notes (trip→departure city, resume→existing resume, tax→residency), meaning the 3B mostly answered \"covered = true\" when it wasn't — it cannot reliably detect the absence of the one dimension it was scoped to. And where it did swap, the replacement was a net negative (buy_used_car gained tangential \"driving preference\"/\"prior car ownership\"; gp gained a presumptuous mobility question replacing the how-to-book channel). This closes the scoped-critique lever alongside the general-audit (exp005) and detect-and-refill (exp017) variants — the entire second-pass-critique family loses, for the same coverage-judgment deficit. exp003/exp011 (~0.32) remains the plateau; the only genuinely untried lever is the weight-level LoRA adapter (not runnable in a single invocation).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"80e5840e-b676-4c3f-84a5-93bdc5b2f283","total_cost_usd":1.5431682500000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":69765,"cache_read_input_tokens":1162346,"output_tokens":21005,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":69765},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":69687,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1462,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":56,"outputTokens":21005,"cacheReadInputTokens":1162346,"cacheCreationInputTokens":69765,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.54260925,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c0d7db3d-4b86-4f99-b556-a5ff97467cbf"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":356027,"duration_api_ms":244756,"ttft_ms":2132,"num_turns":15,"result":"One iteration complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Experiment exp024** — `ragContrastiveFewShot + temp 1.2` (decoding upper endpoint on the best base).\n\n- **Hypothesis:** exp019 isolated the decoding lever's *lower* endpoint (greedy = 0.273, the deterministic floor); the complementary *upper* endpoint was untested. If sharp task-specific unknowns live in the sampling *tail* (exp010's datum), raising temperature to 1.2 on the exp011 contrastive-RAG best base should surface them.\n- **Result: quality 0.267 (dev), spec 100%, 0/0/10 — DISCARDED.** A regression below baseline (0.307), below greedy (0.273), and well below the ~0.32 plateau.\n- **Insight:** The temperature/quality curve is now mapped on the best base — greedy 0.273 → model-default ~0.32 → temp 1.2 = 0.267. **Both endpoints are worse than the model default; the plateau is judgment-limited, not decoding-limited.** High temp didn't surface coverage (stuck at 3, same gaps verbatim) and *added* two new failure modes: atomicity/naturalness degradation (compound, survey-like slots) and catastrophic context leakage (trip_paris emitted \"organize a garage\" questions, bleeding the prepended contrastive demo task). This **closes the decoding lever from both endpoints.**\n\nBuild is green; logged run #25 written to `results/runs.jsonl` and `results/exp024.json`; program.md updated. The log continues to point at the weight-level LoRA adapter as the only genuinely untried lever (not runnable in a single invocation).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"955a2f79-eaa2-4777-b981-41bfd4a1b9c9","total_cost_usd":0.9754314999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62936,"cache_read_input_tokens":373565,"output_tokens":15785,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":62936},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":62287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2033,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2033,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000564,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":15785,"cacheReadInputTokens":373565,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62936,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9748674999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5e590ab6-1f1a-490f-bcef-d91410477676"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":368524,"duration_api_ms":251020,"ttft_ms":2721,"num_turns":22,"result":"Done. One experiment, complete.\n\n**exp025 `ragGivensAware`** — quality **0.287** (dev), spec 100%, 0/0/10, coverage **3**. **DISCARDED** (−0.036 vs best ~0.32, −0.020 vs baseline 0.307).\n\n**Hypothesis:** The most-cited waste in the log is slots spent re-asking facts the task already states. Extracting those GIVENS is an *easy reading task* (unlike exp018's hard \"name the critical unknowns\" judgment that it filled with generic content), so a first in-schema `providedFacts` field + an absolute \"no question may re-ask a given\" rule should free wasted slots for real unknowns — in one coherent draw, no refill pass.\n\n**Result — falsified.** The premise was wrong about *where* the waste goes: the contrastive base rarely burns a whole slot literally restating a given; the waste is on niche/generic unknowns. So freeing givens bought little room, and the model refilled it with the same modal content — the recurring gaps persist verbatim (dinner misses dietary/invited; trip misses departure city/duration; resume misses existing-resume/timeline + a first-person slip; tax stays generic with no Finanzamt/residency). It even added new low-value questions (\"driving preference\", \"join a guitar community\") and fresh dups (resume Q1≈Q5, wedding Q3≈Q4).\n\n**Insight:** It is not the *format* of the first reasoning field (hard-judgment vs easy-extraction) that limits coverage — given any freed capacity, the 3B still picks a generic question over the decision-critical one. This closes the givens-first framing alongside exp018's critical-unknowns-first. The plateau remains exp003/exp011 (~0.32); the only genuinely untried lever is the weight-level LoRA adapter (not runnable in one invocation). Build green; run #26 logged.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ad6aa7e6-6ed5-4c3b-a774-346f8a98ab3a","total_cost_usd":1.5208500000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79716,"cache_read_input_tokens":1223112,"output_tokens":16412,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":79716},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":79169,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":16412,"cacheReadInputTokens":1223112,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79716,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5202910000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"63c1df1a-8dfa-4c5f-9831-4bf69455dcf7"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":450624,"duration_api_ms":201967,"ttft_ms":2410,"num_turns":19,"result":"Done. One experiment, complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**exp026 `ragCompositeBestOfN`** — quality **0.297** (dev), **DISCARDED** (−0.026 vs best exp011 0.323; −0.010 vs baseline 0.307).\n\n**Hypothesis (grounded in exp004's documented failure):** exp004 lost because it ran best-of-N on the weaker exp003 base and selected by a *coverage-only* keyword scorer blind to atomicity/specificity. The log's own unaddressed prescription was \"a useful ruler must score atomicity+specificity+task-fit... and sampling noise needs a low-temp floor.\" So I drew N=4 sets from the **best** generator (exp011 contrastive RAG) with a low-temp floor and selected **fully deterministically** (no 3B judgment) by a **composite ruler** = coverage span − filler − near-dup pairs − compound asks, returning the winner verbatim.\n\n**Result — falsified, with a new finding:**\n1. **Coverage stayed at 3.** Selecting the best of N modal-cluster draws by a quality proxy can't recover a critical unknown no draw produces (exp010's wall holds). The composite ruler *did* buy non-redundancy (nonRed 4) — it works mechanically — but that was never the binding constraint.\n2. **A shape-ruler actively selected a context-leakage draw:** dinner_party emitted 7 questions about *organizing a garage* (the contrastive demo bleeding in at higher temp), and the ruler **preferred** it because garage questions score high on coverage-span with zero defects while being 100% off-task. A deterministic shape-ruler has no task-fit signal, so it can't guard against off-task draws — a risk only multiplied by sampling more.\n\nThis closes the last untried corner of the best-of-N space. The build is green and exactly one new run (#27) is logged. The plateau remains exp003/exp011 (~0.32); the only genuinely untried lever is still the weight-level LoRA adapter, which isn't runnable in a single invocation.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6483cb84-b768-4e09-9e50-5a361307f306","total_cost_usd":1.4356112499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":99749,"cache_read_input_tokens":919892,"output_tokens":14061,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":99749},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":691,"cache_read_input_tokens":98725,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2408,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":14061,"cacheReadInputTokens":919892,"cacheCreationInputTokens":99749,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4350522499999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"fe863940-f597-41eb-b960-11fdf65f1605"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":648080,"duration_api_ms":251480,"ttft_ms":1464,"num_turns":34,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Experiment exp028** — scoped starting-point critique on the champion adapter.\n\n- **Hypothesis (grounded in the champion's own judge notes):** The champion adapter (`adapter_v2a_e1`, 0.409) is strong on atomicity but pinned at coverage 3, and its per-case notes name ONE recurring miss — the user's STARTING POINT / current state (side_business: knows ceramics?; running: medical clearance; resume: existing resume?; trip: departure city). The rules' highest-value untapped lever is re-homing a proven in-context topology ONTO the adapter (higher per-call judgment). So I took exp023's minimal-surface repair — which lost on the stock 3B — and ran it on the champion: Stage 1 = the champion draft verbatim (native adapter format, greedy), Stage 2 = ONE scoped critique judging ONLY starting-point coverage on the adapter, swapping ≤1 weak/redundant slot with filler/near-dup guards.\n\n- **Result: 0.398 (full-30 greedy)** vs champion 0.409 → **−0.011, within noise. DISCARDED.** Coverage stayed pinned at 3; the same starting-point misses recur in the notes.\n\n- **Insight:** The adapter's scoped critique returns \"covered\" too readily and/or its swaps don't add the decision-critical unknown. Adapter per-call judgment, though better in absolute terms, is not reliable enough to self-identify its own single biggest coverage gap via a scoped 2nd pass — the which-unknown-is-critical judgment remains the wall, now confirmed at the adapter+scoped-critique level too.\n\nBuild is green, run #38 logged to `results/runs.jsonl`, `program.md` updated. Champion remains `adapter_v2a_e1` at 0.409.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dfa9ca4a-aecb-4134-b243-26762723ce29","total_cost_usd":1.70083775,"usage":{"input_tokens":99,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123103,"cache_read_input_tokens":997780,"output_tokens":17260,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":123103},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":64658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":691,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":99,"outputTokens":17260,"cacheReadInputTokens":997780,"cacheCreationInputTokens":123103,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.70027875,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"57e29eca-fb59-4e14-b6ba-0ba4f2cd7ad2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":815078,"duration_api_ms":180913,"ttft_ms":1711,"num_turns":31,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Experiment exp029 — divergent→convergent free-text on the champion adapter (untried lever A)**\n\n**Hypothesis:** Every prior call — including all adapter calls — was schema-constrained, forcing the model into 7 typed slots before it could analyze the task. Maybe the schema straitjacket on the *thinking* step is what pins coverage at 3. So: stage 1 = an unconstrained plain-prose brainstorm on the adapter (no `@Generable` schema) about the decision-critical task-specific unknowns; stage 2 = the champion's native-format call conditioned on that prose. Both passes are *generation* (not the judgment that sank exp028), both greedy.\n\n**Result: quality 0.344 (full-30 greedy) — a real −0.065 regression vs champion 0.409. DISCARDED.**\n\n**What the data says:** Freeing the thinking step did NOT lift coverage (still 3) and actively *hurt* specificity (4→3) and naturalness (4→3). Judge notes show the convergence pass regressed toward generic + redundant sets (dinner_party wasted 3 slots on timing; learn_spanish / reading_habit / resume near-dupes). Conditioning the native call on free prose pulled the adapter *off* its tight modal distribution into a looser, more verbose register without surfacing the missing critical unknown.\n\n**Insight:** The schema was not the cause of the coverage wall. The adapter's prose brainstorm names plausible unknowns, but the convergence step neither prioritizes nor reliably transfers them into the 7 slots — the *which-unknown-is-critical selection judgment* remains the wall. Lever A (free-text thinking) now joins lever B (scoped critique, exp028) as a confirmed adapter-side dead end for coverage.\n\nBuild green, exactly one new logged run (exp029), champion unchanged at adapter_v2a_e1 = 0.409.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b92c0654-8693-44